<X3D profile='Interchange' version='4.0' xmlns:xsd='http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance' xsd:noNamespaceSchemaLocation='https://www.web3d.org/specifications/x3d-4.0.xsd'>
<head>
<component name='Shape' level='1'/>
<component name='Grouping' level='2'/>
<meta name='title' content='The sky machine over Giza: horizon, meridian, equator, ecliptic and the path of the pole'/>
<meta name='description' content='Frames of the sky for the star layer of the Giza atlas (Demo 65 v6). Circles of direction drawn on a sphere of radius 9000 light-years, beyond every star in sky.x3d. Axes as sky.x3d: equatorial (x, y, z) stored as X3D (y, z, x). CelLocal and CelEquator are fixed to the stage at latitude 29.979175 N. The page turns CelEcliptic and CelJ2000. The path of the pole is ERFA ltpequ (Vondrak 2011) from 13000 BC to AD 12800, one point every 50 years. Ribbon widths and halos are for the eye: they are not error bars.'/>
<meta name='creator' content='x3d.io Blender pipelines lane for HagopJay'/>
<meta name='generator' content='build_celestial.py (Demo 65 v6)'/>
<meta name='created' content='20 November 2026'/>
<meta name='license' content='GPL-3.0-or-later'/>
</head>
